includes: The AUv3 hosting pillar now actually hosts. In Tools ▸ Plugins, tap one of your installed Audio Unit instruments and Echoel loads it into the live audio graph — then play it from the built-in preview keyboard. A "Loaded" badge shows what's active; Unload removes it. This is the real "host it" step on top of last build's discovery: instantiate the chosen AU, connect it to the master mixer (pause/attach/restart, the same safe path Echoel's own voices use), and drive it with host-MIDI. Stays launch-silent and user-driven — nothing loads or sounds until you tap. Effects insertion, routing the live bio/piano-roll into the hosted instrument, and showing a plugin's own interface are the next steps in this arc. Audio-thread and Swift-6 concurrency reviewed clean. Verified: Xcode Compile Check + CI green.
